Third-party data and libraries keep their own terms:
- SRTM 90 m v4.1 (raw/dem_srtm90_bgd): CGIAR-CSI, free with attribution (Jarvis A., H.I. Reuter, A. Nelson, E. Guevara, 2008)
- ETOPO5 (raw/etopo5_geocat): NOAA NGDC, public domain
- IBTrACS v04r01 (raw/cyclones_ibtracs_ni): NOAA NCEI, public domain
- GPW v4 (raw/pop_gpw4_2015): CIESIN, Columbia University, CC BY 4.0
- GSHHG / WDBII (raw/gshhg_wdbii_basemap): LGPL-3 (Wessel & Smith)
- WFP / LGED major rivers (raw/rivers_wfp_major_rivers_py): open with attribution to WFP GeoNode / LGED
- geoBoundaries ADM1 (raw/adm1.geojson): CC BY 4.0
- ESA WorldCover 2021 (raw/landcover_esa_worldcover2021_bgd, raw/mangroves_worldcover2021_derived, raw/wetlands_haor_aburaihan21 class files): ESA / VITO and partners, CC BY 4.0
- HydroRIVERS v1.0 (raw/rivers_hydrorivers_v10_bgd_dis150): HydroSHEDS licence, free with attribution (Lehner & Grill 2013)
- Global Map Bangladesh river lines via BDmaps (raw/rivers_riverl_bgd_bdmaps): MIT
- OpenStreetMap 2017 water polygons (raw/water_osm_geomaps_2017): ODbL, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors
- Hansen Global Forest Change v1.11 (raw/forest_loss_hansen_cht_2001_2023): CC BY 4.0 (Hansen et al. 2013)
- Haor polygons (raw/wetlands_haor_aburaihan21/haor_hakaluki_tanguar.geojson): thesis digitisation, as published by the author
- FFWC gauge list and river centrelines (raw/gauges_ffwc_kalopathor): compiled from the Flood Forecasting and Warning Centre, as published
- BBS Population and Housing Census 2022 GIS district layer (raw/adm2_districts): Bangladesh Bureau of Statistics, as published; geoBoundaries ADM2: CC BY 4.0
- BBS district population tables (raw/pop_bbs_census_districts): Bangladesh Bureau of Statistics, as published
- Climate series (raw/climate_*): World Bank CCKP / CRU TS country average (CC BY 4.0) via a Kaggle re-host; Bangladesh Meteorological Department station records via the cited compilations (Gauhar et al. 2021; abir-hosen-ashik), as published
- Tide gauges (raw/sea_level_psmsl_bay_of_bengal): PSMSL, free with acknowledgement (Holgate et al. 2013); global mean sea level (raw/sea_level_gmsl_csiro): CSIRO via datasets/sea-level-rise, ODC-PDDL
- Disaster impacts (raw/disasters_emdat_bgd): EM-DAT, CRED / UCLouvain, Brussels, public table, non-commercial use with citation; only the Bangladesh extract is kept
- ERA-Interim 850 hPa winds (raw/wind_erainterim_850hpa_jan_jul): ECMWF, via pydata/xarray-data, not used by the page
- three.js (lib/): MIT; d3 (lib/): ISC; Newsreader, IBM Plex Sans, IBM Plex Mono (assets/fonts): SIL OFL 1.1
